      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(3x-8)(3x+2).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the equation $y=-(3x-8)(3x+2),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{8}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{2}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=1.$",
